instructions:
  - "Boil some water and soak the soya chunks for 10 to 15 minutes."
  - "Now, into a blender, add chopped methi leaves, coriander leaves, ginger, and garlic and blend well."
  - "Cool the soya chunks, squeeze out the excess water, and add to the blender to form a coarse mixture."
  - "Now, add in all the spices as per taste and mix well."
  - "Onto a heated tawa, spread some oil/Ghee and place the soya mixture after shaping them into cutlets."
  - "Flip to the other side once cooked and serve with spiced hung curd or masala dahi."
